  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "supplementary.tex:eq:q4o31phaseratio",
      "statement_sha256": "1d8191b07cee5538c106876243477bdcd6e49f347e4f22c23dca9b7999229259",
      "status": "covered",
      "lean_declarations": [
        "MainTheory.Orbit31PhaseRatios.sigma",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31PhaseRatios.physical_equal_probabilities",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31PhaseRatios.reconstruct",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31PhaseRatios.unit_norm",
        "MainTheory.ComplementPhaseRatios.rho",
        "MainTheory.ComplementPhaseRatios.unit_norm"
      ],
      "review": "20261005 current orbit-31 physical/type review: The actual paired codeword amplitudes have equal squared magnitudes. On an active cell rho=d/star(c) has unit norm; sigma=star(d)/c is its conjugate. Reconstruction star(d)=sigma*c includes zero cells, and unit norm is asserted only on active cells. The physical equality is derived from normalized supported codewords and complete distance-three KL."
    },
    {
      "id": "supplementary.tex:eq:q4o31verticalphase",
      "statement_sha256": "7669ff39eedf6a347862ab1657a30b46578ccba7c731578a0511b5091e8a405c",
      "status": "covered",
      "lean_declarations": [
        "MainTheory.Orbit31CrossConsequences.physical_reciprocal",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31CanonicalPhase.vertical_phase"
      ],
      "review": "20261005 current orbit-31 physical/type review: The twelve actual reciprocal Pauli incidences give equality of phase ratios when both endpoints are active. The retained nonzero hypotheses exclude no boundary solution because zero endpoints carry no phase ratio."
    },
    {
      "id": "supplementary.tex:eq:q4o31weightonesum",
      "statement_sha256": "4ed17ea4b24e1558f74ea341c60d7794c6e5623a19a228a1ae139e1b04420fb8",
      "status": "covered",
      "lean_declarations": [
        "MainTheory.Orbit31CrossConsequences.physical_weight_one_sum",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31CanonicalPhase.weight_one_phase_sum"
      ],
      "review": "20261005 current orbit-31 physical/type review: Conjugating the three physical single-flip cross rows and reconstructing the top amplitudes gives exactly the printed bilinear sums. Terms with zero endpoints vanish automatically."
    },
    {
      "id": "supplementary.tex:eq:q4o31rectangle",
      "statement_sha256": "12fc7408c96a803d5fb065c47c143e18def1f49d4c9134de4dd6a514c2a1408a",
      "status": "covered",
      "lean_declarations": [
        "MainTheory.Orbit31CrossConsequences.physical_rectangles",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31CanonicalPhase.rectangle_phase"
      ],
      "review": "20261005 current orbit-31 physical/type review: All eighteen actual four-term rectangle equations are derived from weight-at-most-two physical Paulis and conjugated into the printed sigma-weighted products. The row and column pairs keep the SI order."
    },
    {
      "id": "supplementary.tex:eq:q4o31supportcounts",
      "statement_sha256": "854f2fd8ec62ffdf27e0aec26da6bfaa29d7891b9e844f98c070c8101e3c707b",
      "status": "covered",
      "lean_declarations": [
        "MainTheory.Orbit31ExactSupportClassification.exact_support_count",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31NoSingletonClassification.exact_support_count",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31PhaseClassification.exact_count_chain",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31PhaseClassification.physical_survivor",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31BalancedMomentIff.feasible_iff_full_moments",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31PhysicalSupportFilters.physical_filters"
      ],
      "review": "20261005 current orbit-31 physical/type review: All 65536 masks have checked primal-union or strict-support dual certificates for arbitrary real nonnegative probabilities in the actual moment system, not only rational points. Exact subtype cardinalities are 15603, 2903 and 311. The actual canonical cross equations rule out singleton overlaps and induce the signed graph. Every remaining graph record has a checked coloring or a checked odd closed walk, and the 2903 records exhaust the first-filter subtype. The seven balanced equations are equivalent to the complete real MomentSystem."
    },
    {
      "id": "supplementary.tex:eq:q4o31symmetry",
      "statement_sha256": "52b94051e43b227fe722845523fb7a3460bcc6c20b8092182955c71aa40d3de5",
      "status": "covered",
      "lean_declarations": [
        "MainTheory.Orbit31AffineTableGroup.aglTwoIsoSFour",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31AffineTableGroup.productGroupIso",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31AffineTableGroup.all_table_actions",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31TableSymmetry.actual_bottom",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31TableSymmetry.actual_top",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31TableSymmetry.fibres_preserved",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31TableSymmetry.inner_preserved",
        "MainTheory.Orbit31TableSymmetry.distance_preserved"
      ],
      "review": "20261005 current orbit-31 physical/type review: The actual affine equivalences of F2 squared form a group isomorphic to all permutations of its four points, with multiplication preserved. Together with the three-row permutation group this gives the printed product group. All 144 table actions are realized by physical qubit permutations and even local-X translations. They preserve both actual fibers, inner products and the complete physical distance condition."
    },
    {
      "id": "supplementary.tex:eq:q4o31permanent",
      "statement_sha256": "9e63029cba12db811249a93acee613d25c3c256206938556682e1d10b8535f76",
      "status": "covered",
      "lean_declarations": [
